=== 1. Download and import commands in this build
Usage: lms get [options] [name]

Search and download local models or Hub artifacts

Arguments:
   name                 The model or Hub artifact to download, for example
                        "openai/gpt-oss-20b" or "owner/my-skill". For a specific model
                        quantization, append its name with "@", for example
                        "qwen/qwen3.5-9b@q8_0". To download a model from Hugging Face
                        directly, use its full URL.

Options:
   --mlx                Restrict model resolution to MLX-compatible options. If any of
                        "--mlx" or "--gguf" is specified, only matching formats will be
                        considered. Otherwise only options supported by your system will
                        be considered.
   --gguf               Restrict model resolution to GGUF-compatible options. If any of
                        "--mlx" or "--gguf" is specified, only matching formats will be
                        considered. Otherwise only options supported by your system will
                        be considered.
   -y, --yes            Automatically approve all prompts. Useful for scripting. If there
                        are multiple staff picks matching the search term, the first one
                        will be used. If there are multiple download options, the
                        preselected option based on your hardware and preferences will be
                        used.
   --select             Open variant selection before downloading. Useful if the default
                        variant is already downloaded and you want to choose a different
                        one.
--- lms import --help
Usage: lms import [options] <file-path>

Import a model file into LM Studio

Arguments:
   file-path                          Path to the model file to import

Options:
   -y, --yes                          Automatically approve all prompts. Will also attempt
                                      to automatically resolve the user and repository
                                      from the file name.
   --user-repo <user/repo>            Manually provide the user and repository in the
                                      format "user/repo". Specifying this will skip
                                      prompts about how to categorize the model file.
   -c, --copy                         Copy the file instead of moving it. This is useful
                                      when you want to keep the original file in place.
   -L, --hard-link                    Create a hard link instead of moving or copying the
                                      file. This is useful when you want to keep the
                                      original file in place.
   -l, --symbolic-link                Create a symbolic link instead of moving or copying
                                      the file. This is useful when you want to keep the
                                      original file in place.
   --dry-run                          Do not actually perform the import, just show what
                                      would be done.

